  "title": "Sorghaghtani Beki",
  "summary": "Sorghaghtani Beki, niece of the Kereit ruler Toghrïl Khan, was given in 1203 as wife to Tolui, Genghis Khan's youngest son, who died in 1233. She held large tracts of land in Hebei Province, China. Her eldest son Möngke was elected khan in 1251, and she died in the winter of 1252.",
